<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-ls2sq8> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25625%2FLS2SQ8>.
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-ls2sq8> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Experimental ftir and raman spectra of dimers of transiently chiral alcohols and (a)chiral hydroxy esters in the range of 3700 and 3300 cm-1".
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-ls2sq8> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "We provide experimental FTIR and Raman spectra of supersonic jet expansions for four systems (all in the range of 3700 and 3300 cm-1): benzyl alcohol + methyl (S)-(-)-lactate, benzyl alcohol + methyl glycolate, 4-chlorobenzyl alcohol + methyl (S)-(-)-lactate, 4-chlorobenzyl alcohol + methyl glycolate. Nomenclature for FTIR spectra: volatile compound_saturator temperature(in °C, \\'m\\' stands for \\'minus\\')_low volatile compound_temperature_nozzle temperature_number of pulses. Nomenclature for Raman spectra: volatile compound_temperature of coolable saturator_low volatile compound_temperature of heatable saturator_backing pressure_nozzle temperature_monochromator wavelength_distance nozzle-laser_laser power_number of exposures x time of single exposure The spectra are provided as data point tables (FTIR) / in the ASCII format (Raman). Columns are separated by commas (FTIR) / tabulators (Raman). The first column corresponds to the wavenumber in cm−1 and the second to the absorbance (FTIR) / intensity in arbitrary units(Raman).".
