<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-gmzz6e> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Provided are the xyz structure files at B3LYP-D3(BJ,abc)/def2-QZVP level for the following dimers: - TEMPO + benzyl alcohol: t, o, p, o\\' - TEMPO + 4-chlorobenzyl alcohol: t, o, p - TEMPO + 2-chlorobenzyl alcohol: o, t, o\\', t\\', o\\'\\' The abbreviations hereby stand for t=tight, o=open, p=plane. The \\' added to o, t and p marks an energetically higher structure with the same structural motif. (See related publication for definition of the structure types)".
