<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-jio1mp> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-jio1mp> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25625%2FJIO1MP>.
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-jio1mp> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Replication data for: embedded trefftz discontinuous galerkin methods".
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-jio1mp> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "This dataset contains reproduction material for the paper \\'Embedded Trefftz discontinuous Galerkin methods\\'. The dataset contains Python files used to produce the results in the paper a docker image with everything pre-installed. To run the python files outside the docker a running installation of NGSolve and NGSTrefftz is required. They are tested with NGSolve@e9e5d06, NGSTrefftz@v0.0.1. The Helmholtz problem additionally uses Hankel functions provided by ngs-special-functions. All the required software and python files are pre-installed and ready to run in the docker image. Start the docker using docker load < ./embtrefftz_docker.tar.gz docker run -it embtrefftz /bin/bash".
