<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-iq2lb6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-iq2lb6> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25625%2FIQ2LB6>.
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-iq2lb6> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Replication data for: losing half the crown hardly affects stem growth: leaf area reduction as climate change adaptation?".
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-iq2lb6> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "We investigate a xeric northern Patagonian Nothofagus pumilio population, in which the majority of trees have damaged crowns, exploring the relationship between percent crown damage and growth trends (basal area increment, BAI), interannual growth variability and the climate sensitivity of growth. This dataset contains the replication data for the main analysis of the manuscript.".
