<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-fqan7u> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "These maps represent the standard deviation of the classification of five different models, trained on different cross-validation splits. The units are arbitrary. Higher values mean that the models did not agree well in a certain location, which can be a hint to degraded classification performance, high temporal dynamics (logging, dying trees) or to a species mix.".
