<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-nmu5p3> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Task-relevant visual feedback uncertainty attenuates visuomotor adaptation".
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-nmu5p3> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "This dataset contains supplementary material and data used for analysis. Supplemental Figure S1: \\'Figure_S1.pdf\\' Supplemental Figure S2: \\'Figure_S2.pdf\\' Supplemental Figure S3: \\'Figure_S3.pdf\\' Supplemental Table S1: \\'Table_S1.pdf\\' Data from Experiment 1 and 2: \\'Experiment_1_data.csv\\' and \\'Experiment_2_data.csv\\' Rows correspond to trials. Columns correspond to: - participant_id: Participant identifier. - uncertainty: Visual feedback uncertainty condition. \\'CRS\\' for cursor (low uncertainty) and \\'CLD\\' for cloud (high uncertainty). - target_direction: Target direction in degrees. - cycle_num: Cycle number. - hit: Whether trial was considered failed during data collection. 0 for failed and 1 for not failed. - condition: Visuomotor rotation block. \\'base\\' for baseline, \\'rot\\' for rotation and \\'wash\\' for washout. - no_fb: Whether visual feedback was provided during reach. 0 for no-feedback and 1 for feedback. - hand_pksp_ang: Hand angle at peak speed of reach in degrees. - rt: Reaction time in ms. - mt: Movement time in ms.".
