<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-gj4pgf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-gj4pgf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25625%2FGJ4PGF>.
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-gj4pgf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Learned ie thesis: comparison of different atmospheric models for helioseismology".
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-gj4pgf> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "This dataset contains intermediate data products for some experiments in the PhD thesis \\'Learned infinite elements for helioseismology\\' (J.Preuß) which compare different models for the solar atmosphere. A brief description of the provided data is given below: The files \\'power-spectrum-VALC-meshed.out\\' and \\'power-spectrum-Atmo-whitw.out\\' contain the power spectrum computed with a meshed VAL-C atmosphere and with the exact Atmo condition obtained by evaluating the Whittaker function, respectively. Harmonic degrees up to l=1000 and 7200 equidistant frequencies ranging from 0.0 mHz up to 8.3 mHz have been computed. The files \\'dtn_nr_VALC_intro.out\\' and \\'dtn_nr_Whitw_intro.out\\' contain the corresponding Dirichlet-to-Neumann numbers (for the Atmo model taken about 500km above the photosphere and for the VAL-C model directly at the photosphere). The file \\'mdi_medium_l.np\\' is a reference power spectrum obtained from satellite observations (HMI). Please see here for the corresponding publication. A description how the computed data has been obtained and how it should be postprocessed further is available at this Gitlab repository.".
