<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-lyr2cg> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Replication data for: analysis of divergence-preserving unfitted finite element methods for the mixed poisson problem".
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-lyr2cg> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Replication Data for: Analysis of divergence-preserving unfitted finite element methods for the mixed Poisson problem Requirement: ngsxfem (version xfem 2.1.2301). Installation instructions are provided at http://github.com/ngsxfem/ngsxfem (easiest is a pip installation) and a docker image is hosted at https://hub.docker.com/r/ngsxfem/ngsxfem . Reproduction instructions: Call the python script \\'unfmixed.py\\' for convergence studies. By default the Dirichlet case and several post-processing versions are active. The parameters are given at the beginning of the script and should be self-explanatory.".
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-lyr2cg> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "goe-doi-10-25625-lyr2cg".
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-lyr2cg> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2023"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-lyr2cg> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://localhost:5002/organization/goettingen>.
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-lyr2cg> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25625/LYR2CG>.
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-lyr2cg> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:goe-doi-10-25625-lyr2cg.
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-lyr2cg> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> "http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0".
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-ezieaw> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-ezieaw> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25625%2FEZIEAW>.
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-ezieaw> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Prevalence of gastrointestinal parasitism in cattle, sheep, and goats across sub-saharan africa: a meta-analysis".
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-ezieaw> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The attached dataset contains the extracted data used in a systematic review and meta-analysis of gastrointestinal parasite (GIP) infections in cattle, sheep, and goats across sub-Saharan Africa. Data were compiled from 117 peer-reviewed studies conducted in 18 countries, identified through a systematic literature search carried out between April and July 2025. For each study, information was extracted on study characteristics (authors, year of publication, country, study design), host species (cattle, sheep, or goats), sample size, number of positive cases, diagnostic methods used, parasite taxa reported, sample source (e.g., on-farm, abattoir, market), and other relevant epidemiological variables. Further details on how the data was generated and cleaned can be found in the methodology section of the afore-mentioned study.".
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-ezieaw> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "goe-doi-10-25625-ezieaw".
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-ezieaw> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2026"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-ezieaw> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://localhost:5002/organization/goettingen>.
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-ezieaw> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25625/EZIEAW>.
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-ezieaw> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:goe-doi-10-25625-ezieaw.
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-ezieaw> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> "http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0".
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-sceqp6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-sceqp6> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25625%2FSCEQP6>.
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-sceqp6> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Replication data for: reinstein and riener (2011) decomposing desert and tangibility effects in a charitable giving experiment".
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-sceqp6> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Several papers have documented that when subjects play with standard laboratory “endowments” they make less self-interested choices than when they use money they have either earned through a laboratory task or brought from outside the lab. In the context of a charitable giving experiment we decompose this into two common artifacts of the laboratory: the intangibility of money (or experimental currency units) promised on a computer screen relative to cash in hand, and the distinct treatment of random “windfall” gains relative to earned money. While both effects are found to be significant in non-parametric tests, the former effect, which has been neglected in previous studies, has a stronger impact on total donations, while the latter effect has a greater impact on the probability of donating. These results have clear implications for experimental design, and also suggest that the availability of more abstract payment methods may increase other-regarding behavior in the field.".
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-sceqp6> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "goe-doi-10-25625-sceqp6".
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-sceqp6> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2022"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime>.
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-sceqp6> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> <http://localhost:5002/organization/goettingen>.
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-sceqp6> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25625/SCEQP6>.
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-sceqp6> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/temporal> _:goe-doi-10-25625-sceqp6.
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-sceqp6> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0".
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-wx473b> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-wx473b> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25625%2FWX473B>.
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-wx473b> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Learned ie thesis: comparison of transparent boundary conditions for the atmo model".
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-wx473b> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "This dataset contains intermediate data products for some experiments in the PhD thesis \\'Learned infinite elements for helioseismology\\' (J.Preuß) which compare different transparent boundary conditions for the Atmo model of the solar atmosphere. A brief description of the provided data is given below: The file \\'power-spectrum-Atmo-whitw-comp.out\\' contains the reference power spectrum obtained from the exact transparent boundary condition for the Atmo model based on evaluation of the Whittaker function. The corresponding dtn numbers (at 500 km above the solar photosphere) are available in the file \\'dtn_nr_Whitw-comp.out\\'. Harmonic degrees up to l=1000 and 2400 equidistant frequencies ranging from 0 mHz up to 12 mHz have been computed. The files \\'power-spectrum-nonlocal.out\\', \\'power-spectrum-SHF1a.out\\' and \\'power-spectrum-ARBC1.out\\' contain the power spectra obtained from the respective atmospheric radiation boundary conditions (i.e. nonlocal, S-HF-1a and A-RBC-1). The corresponding dtn numbers are available in the files \\'dtn_nr_nonlocal.out\\', \\'dtn_nr_S-HF-1a.out\\' and \\'dtn_nr_ARBC1.out\\'. The files \\'power-spectrum-Nj-Atmo.out\\' contain the power spectra computed using learned IEs with N=j for j in [0,1,2,3,4]. The corresponding dtn numbers are available in the files \\'dtn_nr_learned_Nj-Atmo.out\\'. A description how the computed data has been obtained and how it should be postprocessed further is available at this Gitlab repository.".
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-wx473b> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "goe-doi-10-25625-wx473b".
