<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-xn7lqy> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25625%2FXN7LQY>.
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-xn7lqy> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Replication data for: ecosystem processes show uniform sensitivity to winter soil temperature change across a gradient from central to cold-marginal stands of a major temperate forest tree".
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-xn7lqy> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "We conducted a gradient-design snow cover and soil temperature manipulation experiment across a range of lowland beech forest sites to assess the site-specific sensitivity of tree growth and biogeochemical cycling to soil cooling. Even mild and inconsistent soil frost affected tree increment, germination, litter decomposition and the retention of added 15 N.".
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-xn7lqy> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "goe-doi-10-25625-xn7lqy".
