<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-imudzi> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25625%2FIMUDZI>.
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-imudzi> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Metadata for publication \\'the general movement optimality score-revised (gmos-r) with socioeconomically stratified percentile ranks\\'".
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-imudzi> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "This paper is based on general movement optimality score - revised (GMOS-R) ratings of non public infant video recordings. We applied the GMOS-R to an international sample of 1983 infants (32% female, 44% male, and 24% not disclosed), assessed in the extremely and very preterm period (10%), moderate (12%) and late (22%) preterm periods, at term (25%), and post-term age (31%).".
