<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-o95f9s> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#Dataset>.
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-o95f9s> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://doi.org/10.25625%2FO95F9S>.
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-o95f9s> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Sensorimotor environment but not task rule reconfigures population dynamics in rhesus monkey posterior parietal cortex".
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-o95f9s> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The dataset consists of several hundred single-neuron recordings from multiple rhesus monkeys performing visually guided reaching tasks. It was designed to test whether changes in the environment (sensorimotor feedback) and changes in abstract rule context engage shared or distinct population-level neural mechanisms in the PPC. Detailed Information about the data fields in this publication: DovePrism_: numT: number of trials, matrix of size unit*condition psthTT: trial-by-trial psth, cell of size unit*condition, in each cell, trial*time psthTA: trial-averaged psth, matrix of size unit*time*condition sequence of task conditions: normal left, normal right, prism left, prism right Prism+Anti_: same as DovePrism_ sequence of task conditions: normal pro left, normal pro right, prism pro left, prism pro right, normal anti left, normal anti right, prism anti left, prism anti right PA_: numT: number of trials, matrix of size unit*direction*mapping*cuing psthTT: trial-by-trial psth, cell of size unit*direction*mapping*cuing, in each cell, trial*time psthTA: trial-averaged psth, matrix of size unit*time*direction*mapping*cuing sequence of direction: left right up down sequence of mapping: pro anti sequence of cuing: ECES LCLS ECLS LCES _g20psth datasets: bin: 10 ms kernel: 20 ms The analysis time window is [-800 800] ms aligned to onset of the visual cue. _g50psth datasets: bin: 10 ms kernel: 50 ms The analysis time window is [-200 800] ms aligned to onset of the visual cue.".
