<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-dqjtzo> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Evidence on the effectiveness-acceptance trade-off between forced active choice and default nudging - a field study to reduce meat consumption in cafeterias".
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-dqjtzo> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Cafeteria intervention of meat dishes: -Field Experiment in a health clinic -11 intervention dishes over 3 experimental conditions spanning 6 weeks for each condition -manual recording of dish choices between reduced meat portion, standard meat portion, vegetarian dish, including choice for side-dishes, time, gender and intervention day information -Follow up survey in cafeteria on acceptance for interventions".
<http://localhost:5002/goe-doi-10-25625-dqjtzo> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "goe-doi-10-25625-dqjtzo".
